IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ga-dates`

-- Guardianship Act 1987 (NSW) -- Part 2, appointment of enduring guardians (ss 5-6O), from the seat of the appointor.
--
-- SEAT: the person who appoints (or wants to appoint) an enduring guardian, and who may later lose capacity. Every
-- exported question is one that person would ask: "Can I appoint one?", "Can this person be my enduring guardian?", "Does
-- my document work?", "Does the appointment have effect now?", "What can my enduring guardian decide?", "How do I revoke
-- it?", "Can they resign?", "When does my substitute step in?", "Can the Tribunal revoke it or appoint a substitute?",
-- "Does my interstate appointment work here?". The appointee, the Tribunal and the Supreme Court get no seat.
--
-- ANSWERS. JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("does not operate ... unless", "has effect only",
-- "is not eligible", "only if", a flat "is of no effect"); NOTHING, with a NOTHING-kind comment, where it does not
-- answer. The Tribunal's judgments ("satisfied", "genuine concern", "best interests") are asked as facts.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 27 March 2021; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guardianship Act 1987 -- Part 2 enduring guardians`

§§ `ss 6, 6I(2) -- can I appoint an enduring guardian`

-- s 6 "A person of or above the age of 18 years may, by instrument in writing, appoint a person as his or her guardian."
-- s 6I(2) "If a person who is the subject of a guardianship order purports to appoint an enduring guardian, the purported
-- appointment is of no effect." s 6I(3): a guardianship order includes a Supreme Court order and a corresponding-law
-- order to the like effect. A person under 18 is outside the grant, which has no "only": NOTHING (fork F4).
@export Can I appoint an enduring guardian on this day (ss 6, 6I(2))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day I would sign the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The day you would sign the instrument appointing the enduring guardian
      `a guardianship order is in force about me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guardianship order is in force about you (made by the NSW Civil and Administrative Tribunal, the Supreme Court, or under a corresponding law of another State, Territory or country)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I appoint an enduring guardian` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a guardianship order is in force about me` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6I(2) "is of no effect"
           IF `born on` `my date of birth` `is at least` 18 `years old on` `the day I would sign the appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited in its own wording, "of or above the age of 18 years", with no "only"; fork F4)

§§ `s 6B -- who may be my enduring guardian`

-- s 6B(1) "A person is not eligible to be appointed as an enduring guardian unless he or she is of or above the age of
-- 18 years." s 6B(2) "A person is not eligible ... if-- (a) the person is, in a professional or administrative
-- capacity, directly or indirectly responsible for, or involved in, the provision of any of the following services for
-- fee or reward to the person making the appointment-- (i) medical services ..., (ii) accommodation, (iii) any other
-- services to support the person making the appointment in his or her activities of daily living, or (b) the person is
-- the spouse, parent, child, brother or sister of a person of the kind referred to in paragraph (a)." Each bar is the
-- text's no. Where no bar applies the Act has no other: JUST TRUE (fork F5).
@export Is this person eligible to be appointed as my enduring guardian (s 6B(1), (2))?
GIVEN `their date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person you want to appoint
      `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The day the appointment is made
      `they provide paid medical, accommodation or daily-living services to me in a professional or administrative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on that day, the person is, in a professional or administrative capacity, directly or indirectly responsible for or involved in providing to you, for fee or reward, medical services, accommodation, or other services supporting your activities of daily living
      `they are the spouse, parent, child, brother or sister of someone who does` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on that day, the person is the spouse, parent, child, brother or sister of someone who is responsible for or involved in providing those services to you in that way
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is this person eligible to be my enduring guardian` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`born on` `their date of birth` `is at least` 18 `years old on` `the day of the appointment`)) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6B(1) "not eligible ... unless"
           IF `they provide paid medical, accommodation or daily-living services to me in a professional or administrative capacity` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6B(2)(a)
           IF `they are the spouse, parent, child, brother or sister of someone who does` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6B(2)(b)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- no bar in the Act applies (fork F5)

-- s 6B(3) "However, if a person who is validly appointed as an enduring guardian becomes responsible for or involved in
-- the provision for fee or reward of a service to the appointor of the kind referred to in subsection (2) (a), the
-- appointment does not lapse." A flat "does not lapse". Where the appointment was not valid in the first place, s 6B(3)
-- does not speak: NOTHING.
@export My enduring guardian has since begun providing me paid medical, accommodation or daily-living services: does the appointment lapse (s 6B(3))?
GIVEN `I validly appointed them before they began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person was validly appointed as your enduring guardian before they became responsible for or involved in providing those services to you for fee or reward
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the appointment lapse because my enduring guardian began providing paid services` MEANS
    IF `I validly appointed them before they began`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6B(3) "the appointment does not lapse"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 6B(3) speaks only of a valid appointment; an invalid one never operated)

§§ `ss 5, 6C, 6I(2), 6K(4), (5) -- does my appointment document work`

-- s 6C(1) "An instrument does not operate to appoint a person as an enduring guardian unless-- (a) it is in or to the
-- effect of the form prescribed by the regulations, and (b) it is signed-- (i) by the appointor, or (ii) if the appointor
-- instructs--by an eligible signer who signs for the appointor in the appointor's presence, and (c) it is endorsed with
-- the appointee's acceptance of the appointment, and (d) the execution of the instrument by the appointor and appointee is
-- witnessed by one or more eligible witnesses, and (e) each witness certifies that the person or persons whose execution
-- of the instrument is witnessed executed the instrument voluntarily in the presence of the witness and appeared to
-- understand the effect of the instrument, and (f) if the instrument is signed for the appointor by an eligible signer--
-- the person who witnesses the signature certifies that the appointor, in the witness's presence, instructed the signer
-- to sign the instrument for the appointor." s 6C(2): a mark is a signature.
-- s 5 eligible signer: at least 18, not a witness, not an appointee or substitute enduring guardian. Eligible witness: an
-- Australian legal practitioner, a registrar of the Local Court, or a person prescribed by the regulations (the
-- Guardianship Regulation is not deposited), and not an appointee or substitute enduring guardian.
-- s 6K(4), (5): the Tribunal may confirm an appointment that was not executed as Part 2 requires, and the confirmation has
-- effect as if the instrument had been properly executed.
DECLARE `How the appointment was signed` IS ONE OF
    `I signed it myself, or made my mark`
    `an eligible signer signed it for me, at my instruction and in my presence`
    `it was signed in some other way, or not at all`

DECLARE `The kind of witness` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian legal practitioner`
    `a registrar of the Local Court`
    `a person prescribed by the regulations`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `the kind of witness` IS A `The kind of witness`
      `the witness is an appointee or substitute enduring guardian` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an eligible witness` `the kind of witness` `the witness is an appointee or substitute enduring guardian` IF
        (CONSIDER `the kind of witness`
         WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND (NOT `the witness is an appointee or substitute enduring guardian`)

@export Does the document I signed operate to appoint my enduring guardian (ss 5, 6, 6C, 6I(2), 6K(4), (5))?
GIVEN `I was at least 18 when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were 18 or older when you made the appointment
      `a guardianship order was in force about me when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guardianship order (of the Tribunal, the Supreme Court, or under a corresponding law) was in force about you when you made it
      `it is in or to the effect of the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document is in, or to the effect of, the form prescribed by the Guardianship Regulation
      `how it was signed` IS A `How the appointment was signed` @desc How the document was signed for you. One of: "I signed it myself, or made my mark", "an eligible signer signed it for me, at my instruction and in my presence", "it was signed in some other way, or not at all"
      `the signer was at least 18, not a witness, and not an appointee or substitute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone signed for you: whether that signer was 18 or older, was not a witness to the document, and was not an appointee or substitute enduring guardian (answer yes if you signed it yourself)
      `the appointee endorsed their acceptance on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person appointed endorsed their acceptance of the appointment on the document
      `the kind of witness` IS A `The kind of witness` @desc Who witnessed your signing and the appointee's signing (if different witnesses, the one least clearly qualified). One of: "an Australian legal practitioner", "a registrar of the Local Court", "a person prescribed by the regulations", "someone else"
      `a witness is an appointee or substitute enduring guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any witness is a person appointed by the document as enduring guardian or substitute enduring guardian
      `each witness certified voluntary signing in their presence and apparent understanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether each witness certified that the person whose signing they witnessed signed voluntarily, in the witness's presence, and appeared to understand the effect of the document
      `the witness certified my instruction to the signer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone signed for you: whether the witness to that signature certified that you, in the witness's presence, instructed the signer to sign for you (answer yes if you signed it yourself)
      `the Tribunal has confirmed the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal, on reviewing the appointment, has confirmed it (it can do so even if the document was not properly made, if satisfied the confirmation reflects the appointment you intended)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my appointment document operate` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the Tribunal has confirmed the appointment` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 6K(5) "has effect as if an instrument ... had been executed in accordance with the requirements"
           IF `a guardianship order was in force about me when I made it` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6I(2) "is of no effect"
           IF (NOT `I was at least 18 when I made it`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside the s 6 grant, which has no "only"; fork F4)
           IF `formalities met` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 6C(1) "does not operate ... unless"
    WHERE
        `signed as required` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how it was signed`
            WHEN `I signed it myself, or made my mark` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an eligible signer signed it for me, at my instruction and in my presence` THEN `the signer was at least 18, not a witness, and not an appointee or substitute` AND `the witness certified my instruction to the signer`
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `formalities met` MEANS
                `it is in or to the effect of the prescribed form`
            AND `signed as required`
            AND `the appointee endorsed their acceptance on it`
            AND `an eligible witness` `the kind of witness` `a witness is an appointee or substitute enduring guardian`
            AND `each witness certified voluntary signing in their presence and apparent understanding`

§§ `ss 6A, 6H, 6HA, 6HC, 6I(1), 6J(3), 6K -- does the appointment have effect now`

-- s 6A(1) "An appointment under this Part-- (a) has effect only during such period of time as the appointor is a person in
-- need of a guardian, and (b) unless revoked or suspended under this Part, has effect during all such periods."
-- s 6HA "The appointment ... is revoked if the appointor marries or remarries a person (other than the appointee) after the
-- date on which the person was appointed". s 6HC saves certain appointments on the recognition of same-sex marriages
-- (asked as a fact). s 6I(1): a guardianship order "operates to suspend, for the duration of the order, all authority of
-- the enduring guardian". s 6J(3): the Tribunal may suspend pending its review; s 6K(1)(a): it may revoke.
-- s 3C(3): for a patient under the Mental Health Act 2007 the appointment is effective only so far as consistent with
-- orders under that Act (a comment; asked nowhere, since it narrows rather than ends the appointment).
DECLARE `Where my enduring guardian's appointment stands` IS ONE OF
    `it has effect now`
    `it does not have effect now, because I am not a person in need of a guardian`
    `it is suspended while a guardianship order is in force about me`
    `it is suspended by the Tribunal pending its review`
    `it has been revoked`

@export Does my enduring guardian's appointment have effect now (ss 6A, 6H, 6HA, 6HC, 6I(1), 6J(3), 6K)?
GIVEN `I am now a person in need of a guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now, because of a disability, totally or partially incapable of managing your person
      `I have revoked it by a document that complies with section 6H` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have revoked the appointment by a properly made revocation (see the revocation question), with written notice given to the appointee
      `I married or remarried someone other than the appointee after the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the day of the appointment, you married or remarried a person other than the enduring guardian
      `section 6HC saves the appointment from that marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the marriage was a same-sex marriage solemnised before, and recognised in Australia only on, the day the Commonwealth Marriage Amendment (Definition and Religious Freedoms) Act 2017 recognised it, and you have made no later appointment (s 6HC)
      `the Tribunal has revoked the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal (or the Supreme Court) has revoked the appointment
      `a guardianship order is in force about me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guardianship order (of the Tribunal, the Supreme Court, or under a corresponding law) is in force about you
      `the Tribunal has suspended the appointment pending its review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has suspended the appointment until it finishes reviewing it
GIVETH A `Where my enduring guardian's appointment stands`
`Does my enduring guardian's appointment have effect now` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I have revoked it by a document that complies with section 6H` THEN `it has been revoked`
           IF `I married or remarried someone other than the appointee after the appointment` AND (NOT `section 6HC saves the appointment from that marriage`) THEN `it has been revoked`
           IF `the Tribunal has revoked the appointment` THEN `it has been revoked`
           IF `a guardianship order is in force about me` THEN `it is suspended while a guardianship order is in force about me`
           IF `the Tribunal has suspended the appointment pending its review` THEN `it is suspended by the Tribunal pending its review`
           IF `I am now a person in need of a guardian` THEN `it has effect now`
           OTHERWISE `it does not have effect now, because I am not a person in need of a guardian`

§§ `ss 6E, 6F, 6G -- what my enduring guardian can decide`

-- s 6E(1) "an instrument appointing a person as an enduring guardian authorises the appointee, while the appointment has
-- effect, to exercise the following functions-- (a) deciding the place ... in which the appointor is to live, (b) deciding
-- the health care that the appointor is to receive, (c) deciding the other kinds of personal services that the appointor
-- is to receive, (d) giving consent under Part 5 to the carrying out of medical or dental treatment on the appointor, (e)
-- any other function relating to the appointor's person that is specified in the instrument." s 6E(2) "The instrument of
-- appointment may limit or exclude the authority". s 6G: the enduring guardian's decisions have effect as if made by the
-- appointor with legal capacity. Money and property (the "estate") are not a function relating to the person; s 6E does
-- not list them, but its list is not closed with "only": NOTHING (fork F6). "While the appointment has effect" is a
-- period the text fixes: outside it, JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `The decision` IS ONE OF
    `where I live`
    `the health care I receive`
    `the other personal services I receive`
    `consent under Part 5 to medical or dental treatment on me`
    `another function relating to my person that my instrument specifies`
    `managing my money or property`
    `something else my instrument does not specify`

@export Can my enduring guardian make this decision for me (ss 6E, 6G)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision you are asking about. One of: "where I live", "the health care I receive", "the other personal services I receive", "consent under Part 5 to medical or dental treatment on me", "another function relating to my person that my instrument specifies", "managing my money or property", "something else my instrument does not specify"
      `the appointment has effect now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the appointment has effect now (see the question on whether it has effect: you must be in need of a guardian, and it must not be revoked or suspended)
      `my instrument excludes or limits this decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your appointment document excludes, or limits so as to leave out, this decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my enduring guardian make this decision` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the appointment has effect now`) THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6E(1) "while the appointment has effect"
           IF `my instrument excludes or limits this decision` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6E(2)
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the decision`
               WHEN `managing my money or property` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 6E(1) lists without "only"; money is not a function relating to the person; fork F6)
               WHEN `something else my instrument does not specify` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 6E(1) lists without "only")
               OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 6H -- revoking the appointment`

-- s 6H(2) "An instrument does not operate to revoke the appointment of an enduring guardian unless-- (a) at the time of
-- executing the instrument, the appointor had the legal capacity to revoke the appointment, and (b) ... the form
-- prescribed by the regulations, and (c) ... signed-- (i) by the appointor, or (ii) if the appointor instructs--by an
-- eligible signer ..., and (c1) ... witnessed by an eligible witness, and (c2) the eligible witness certifies that the
-- appointor executed the instrument voluntarily ... and appeared to understand the effect ..., and (c3) if ... signed for
-- the appointor by an eligible signer--the eligible witness certifies that the appointor ... instructed the signer ...,
-- and (d) written notice of the revocation is given to the appointee." Legal capacity is the general law's (asked).
@export Does my document revoke my enduring guardian's appointment (ss 5, 6H)?
GIVEN `I had legal capacity to revoke when I signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you signed the revocation, you had the legal capacity to revoke the appointment
      `it is in or to the effect of the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the revocation is in, or to the effect of, the form prescribed by the Guardianship Regulation
      `how it was signed` IS A `How the appointment was signed` @desc How the revocation was signed for you. One of: "I signed it myself, or made my mark", "an eligible signer signed it for me, at my instruction and in my presence", "it was signed in some other way, or not at all"
      `the signer was at least 18, not a witness, and not an appointee or substitute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone signed for you: whether that signer was 18 or older, was not the witness, and was not an appointee or substitute enduring guardian (answer yes if you signed it yourself)
      `the kind of witness` IS A `The kind of witness` @desc Who witnessed your signing. One of: "an Australian legal practitioner", "a registrar of the Local Court", "a person prescribed by the regulations", "someone else"
      `the witness is an appointee or substitute enduring guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witness is the enduring guardian or a substitute enduring guardian
      `the witness certified voluntary signing in their presence and apparent understanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witness certified that you signed voluntarily, in the witness's presence, and appeared to understand the effect of the revocation
      `the witness certified my instruction to the signer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone signed for you: whether the witness certified that you, in the witness's presence, instructed the signer to sign (answer yes if you signed it yourself)
      `written notice of the revocation was given to the appointee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether written notice of the revocation has been given to the enduring guardian
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my revocation operate` MEANS
    IF     `I had legal capacity to revoke when I signed`
       AND `it is in or to the effect of the prescribed form`
       AND `signed as required`
       AND `an eligible witness` `the kind of witness` `the witness is an appointee or substitute enduring guardian`
       AND `the witness certified voluntary signing in their presence and apparent understanding`
       AND `written notice of the revocation was given to the appointee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 6H(2) "does not operate to revoke ... unless"
    WHERE
        `signed as required` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how it was signed`
            WHEN `I signed it myself, or made my mark` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an eligible signer signed it for me, at my instruction and in my presence` THEN `the signer was at least 18, not a witness, and not an appointee or substitute` AND `the witness certified my instruction to the signer`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 6HB -- my enduring guardian resigning`

-- s 6HB(1) "An appointee may resign the appointee's appointment as an enduring guardian-- (a) if the appointor is not in
-- need of a guardian--by giving written notice to that effect to the appointor, or (b) if the appointor is in need of a
-- guardian--with the approval of the Tribunal." s 6HB(2): the notice must be in the prescribed form, signed, and
-- witnessed by an eligible witness (with a certificate where an eligible signer signs). s 6HB(5): the same for a
-- substitute. Conditions introduced by "if": a failed one is JUST FALSE.
@export Has my enduring guardian (or substitute) validly resigned (s 6HB)?
GIVEN `I am in need of a guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, because of a disability, totally or partially incapable of managing your person
      `they gave me written notice of resignation that complies with section 6HB(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they gave you a written notice of resignation in the prescribed form, signed by them (or an eligible signer at their instruction), and witnessed by an eligible witness
      `the Tribunal approved the resignation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has approved their resignation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Has my enduring guardian validly resigned` MEANS
    IF `I am in need of a guardian`
    THEN IF `the Tribunal approved the resignation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 6HB(1)(b)
    ELSE IF `they gave me written notice of resignation that complies with section 6HB(2)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 6HB(1)(a), (2)

§§ `s 6DA -- my substitute enduring guardian`

-- s 6DA(2) "The instrument of appointment does not operate to appoint a person as a substitute enduring guardian unless
-- it is endorsed with the person's acceptance of the appointment." s 6DA(3) "A substitute enduring guardian has (and may
-- exercise) the functions of an original enduring guardian only-- (a) if the original enduring guardian dies, or (b) ...
-- resigns, or (c) during any incapacity of the original enduring guardian." A list closed with "only": JUST FALSE outside.
DECLARE `My original enduring guardian` IS ONE OF
    `has died`
    `has resigned`
    `is incapacitated`
    `is alive, has not resigned and is not incapacitated`

@export Can my substitute enduring guardian act for me now (s 6DA(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the substitute endorsed their acceptance on my instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the substitute enduring guardian endorsed their acceptance of the appointment on your appointment document
      `my original enduring guardian` IS A `My original enduring guardian` @desc Where your original enduring guardian stands. One of: "has died", "has resigned", "is incapacitated", "is alive, has not resigned and is not incapacitated"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my substitute enduring guardian act for me now` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the substitute endorsed their acceptance on my instrument`)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6DA(2) "does not operate ... unless"
    ELSE CONSIDER `my original enduring guardian`
         WHEN `is alive, has not resigned and is not incapacitated` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 6DA(3) "only"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 6J, 6K, 6MA -- the Tribunal and my appointment`

-- s 6J(1) "The Tribunal-- (a) may, on its own motion, and (b) must, at the request of any person who, in the opinion of
-- the Tribunal, has a genuine concern for the welfare of the appointor, review the appointment". Without such a request
-- the Tribunal "may": NOTHING.
@export If someone asks, must the Tribunal review my enduring guardian's appointment (s 6J(1))?
GIVEN `the Tribunal considers the person asking has a genuine concern for my welfare` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is of the opinion that the person asking for the review (which can be you) has a genuine concern for your welfare
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the Tribunal review my enduring guardian's appointment` MEANS
    IF `the Tribunal considers the person asking has a genuine concern for my welfare`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 6J(1)(b) "must"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the Tribunal "may" review on its own motion; the Act does not decide whether it will)

-- s 6K(2) "The Tribunal must not revoke the appointment of an enduring guardian unless-- (a) the enduring guardian
-- requested the revocation, or (b) the Tribunal is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the appointor that the
-- appointment be revoked."
@export On reviewing my enduring guardian's appointment, can the Tribunal revoke it (s 6K(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my enduring guardian asked for the revocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your enduring guardian asked for the appointment to be revoked
      `the Tribunal is satisfied revocation is in my best interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that revoking the appointment is in your best interests
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal revoke my enduring guardian's appointment` MEANS
    IF `my enduring guardian asked for the revocation` OR `the Tribunal is satisfied revocation is in my best interests`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 6K(1)(a) "may revoke"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 6K(2) "must not revoke ... unless"

-- s 6MA(1) The Tribunal may appoint a substitute enduring guardian "if the appointee has died, resigned or become
-- incapacitated". s 6MA(2) "The Tribunal may appoint a person under subsection (1) only if-- (a) the person is eligible to
-- be appointed as an enduring guardian under this Part, and (b) the Tribunal is satisfied that-- (i) the appointor is in
-- need of an enduring guardian, and (ii) the person has a close personal relationship with the appointor, and (iii) the
-- person is capable of carrying out the functions of an enduring guardian."
@export My enduring guardian has died, resigned or become incapacitated: can the Tribunal appoint this person as my substitute (s 6MA)?
GIVEN `my enduring guardian has died, resigned or become incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your enduring guardian has died, resigned or become incapacitated
      `the person is eligible to be an enduring guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proposed person is eligible under s 6B (18 or older, and not a paid provider of your medical, accommodation or daily-living services, or a close relative of one)
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of an enduring guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that you are in need of an enduring guardian
      `the Tribunal is satisfied the person has a close personal relationship with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that the proposed person has a close personal relationship with you
      `the Tribunal is satisfied the person can carry out the functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that the proposed person is capable of carrying out the functions of an enduring guardian
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal appoint this person as my substitute enduring guardian` MEANS
    IF     `my enduring guardian has died, resigned or become incapacitated`
       AND `the person is eligible to be an enduring guardian`
       AND `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of an enduring guardian`
       AND `the Tribunal is satisfied the person has a close personal relationship with me`
       AND `the Tribunal is satisfied the person can carry out the functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 6MA(1) "if", (2) "only if"

§§ `s 6O -- an enduring guardian appointed in another State or Territory`

-- s 6O(1) "An instrument appointing an interstate enduring guardian has effect in this State as if it were an instrument
-- appointing an enduring guardian made under, and in compliance with, this Part, but only to the extent that the
-- functions it confers under the law of the State or Territory in which it was made could validly have been conferred by
-- an instrument appointing an enduring guardian made under this Part." s 6O(2)(b): it "does not operate to confer any
-- function ... that cannot be conferred ... under this Part". s 6O(5): the instrument must be of a kind prescribed by the
-- regulations (not deposited; asked).
@export I appointed my guardian in another State or Territory: does that appointment work in NSW for this function (s 6O)?
GIVEN `the instrument is of a kind prescribed by the regulations under another State or Territory law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your appointment was made under the law of another Australian State or Territory by an instrument of a kind prescribed by the NSW Guardianship Regulation
      `the function could be conferred on an enduring guardian under Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the function you are asking about (for example deciding where you live, or consenting to treatment) is one that a NSW enduring guardian appointment could confer
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my interstate appointment work in NSW` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the instrument is of a kind prescribed by the regulations under another State or Territory law`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside s 6O; the prescribed kinds are in a regulation not deposited)
           IF `the function could be conferred on an enduring guardian under Part 2` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- s 6O(1) "but only to the extent", (2)(b) "does not operate to confer"
